,J)$ with $q=-j^2/N$ to obtain $\\widehat\\alpha_j$, and set $a_j=\\operatorname{fl}_{\\mathbb C}(\\widehat\\alpha_jx_j)$; set the remaining entries of $a\\in\\mathbb C^M$ to zero. For each $-(N-1)\\le t\\le N-1$, obtain $\\widehat\\beta_t$ by the same call with $q=t^2/N$ and set $b_{[t]_M}=\\widehat\\beta_t$, setting other entries of $b$ to zero. Compute the cyclic convolution with [[alg-na-computed-fft-cyclic-and-linear-convolution]] in `cyclic` mode using controls $(\\tau,e_{\\min},e_{\\max},p_0,p_{\\max},J,d_{\\max})$. For each $0\\le k<N$, obtain $\\widehat\\gamma_k$ by the same phase call with $q=-k^2/N$ and set $\\widehat X_k=\\operatorname{fl}_{\\mathbb C}(\\widehat\\gamma_k\\widehat c_k)$. Return the first $N$ entries or the first failure status.\n\nThe divisor search and phase-enclosure work have separate integer/interval budgets and are not counted as complex arithmetic operations in the operation-count theorem. The exact factorization lemmas and the chirp-phase error theorem state what is guaranteed; this procedure by itself makes no general mixed-radix stability claim.",
